# Iris Dataset Analysis 🌸

In this notebook, I analyzed the Iris dataset using Python and explored the relationship between petal length and petal width across three different Iris species.

## Dataset

The Iris dataset contains information about three species of Iris flowers:
- Setosa
- Versicolor
- Virginica

Each sample includes features such as:
- Sepal length
- Sepal width
- Petal length
- Petal width

## Tools & Libraries

- Python
- Pandas
- Matplotlib
- Scikit-learn

## Analysis

In this project, I performed:
- Data loading and exploration
- Statistical analysis
- Data visualization
- Scatter plot analysis of petal features

## Visualization

The scatter plot shows the relationship between petal length and petal width, with different colors representing the three Iris species.

## Conclusion

The visualization shows that petal measurements can help distinguish between different Iris species, as some species form clearly separated groups based on their petal features.
